{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1476599-aberrant-tech-control-hacking-in-powers","id":1476599,"title":"[Aberrant] - Tech Control/Hacking in Powers?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-03-17T13:59:52-07:00","id":1476599,"title":"[Aberrant] - Tech Control/Hacking in Powers?","content":"Short version: Psions have some pretty robust tech control from Electrokinesis in particular, things that let them control or hack devices with supernal ease. I've struggled trying to find an equivalent skill or power for Novas that give them a similar efficacy with controlling or hacking tech. Is there an Edge (mega or otherwise), or Quantum Power that would cover this area?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24767-navah","name":"Navah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-17T14:19:33-07:00","id":1476600,"title":"","content":"The Mega-Edges Digital Manipulation and Digital Scan let your character control electronic devices and read info from their hard drives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-17T17:24:35-07:00","id":1476611,"title":"","content":"One Dot <b>Mega-Intelligence</b>: 12pts<br /> One Dot <b>Mega-Cunning</b>: 12pts<br /> One Dot <b>Digital Manipulation</b>: 12pts<br /> One Dot <b>Digital Scan</b>: 12pts<br /> <br /> Assuming you have a decent <b>Intellect</b> attribute score and some dots in the <b>Technology</b> skill - that's 48pts (out of your allowed 150pts starting nova). That lets you control electronic devices (including computers) within Close range and read data from them (more secure devices / harder encryption need more successes on the Intellect+Technology roll).<br /> <br /> <u><b>Dev Note/Question Here:</b></u><br /> Not exactly sure why there is the option of buying extra dots in <b>Digital Manipulation</b> (12pts per dot) when the only benefit given is substituting for <b>Intellect</b> (10pts per dot) or <b>Technology</b> (5pts per dot) in the above roll. It is straight up better to just buy the one dot of Mega-Edge and pay XP to improve Intellect/Technology instead. Was there something cut out of the power in editing?<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1476612#post1476612\">Asked question in Dev Thread</a>. Will copy across answer if/when devs respond.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26905,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","user":"Eternl Knight","date":". 03-17-2022, 08:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-17T18:59:34-07:00","id":1476622,"title":"","content":"It does seem to be slightly broken. Slightly. If you take a Transformation with Digital Manipulation, you can lower its cost per dot to 9, 6, or 3; 9 or 6 makes it cheaper than Intellect, while 3 makes it cheaper than Technology. But since you need at least as many dots in Mega-Intellect as your Digital Manipulation, and at least as many dots in Intellect as Mega-Intellect, you'll never have enough dots in Digital Manipulation to substitute for Intellect. <br /> <br /> House rule: you never need more than one dot in Mega-Intellect to unlock Digital Manipulation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-17T19:43:58-07:00","id":1476625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1476599-aberrant-tech-control-hacking-in-powers?p=1476622#post1476622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But since you need at least as many dots in Mega-Intellect as your Digital Manipulation, and at least as many dots in Intellect as Mega-Intellect, you'll never have enough dots in Digital Manipulation to substitute for Intellect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Missed that, but that's another oddity. Slipped by me because, as mentioned above, the math for buying extra dots in the Mega-Edge wasn't worth it compared to just levelling up the basic Attribute or Skill. But yeah, there is no way for Digital Manipulation to be higher than Intellect, so there is no point at all to it being able to substitute for it. Another thing that makes me think that something with this power got edited close to the print date and there is a mistake here.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-18T02:05:25-07:00","id":1476637,"title":"","content":"It is one of the powers that was a bit off even before, in the KS Manuscript. I think we had this discussion about how it would not worth any dots after the first.<br /> <br /> Who ever wrote it, didn\u2019t expressed well on out it\u2019s utility or it\u2019s utility was cut from the text long before printing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-18T07:27:31-07:00","id":1476656,"title":"","content":"Another possible fix would be to say that you can substitute <i>double</i> the Digital Manipulation rating for either Intellect or Technology. In either case, once you have three dots in Digital Manipulation, it no longer matters how much Intellect or Technology costs: they <i>top out</i> at five dice, while Digital Manipulation 3 would give six dice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-18T11:46:21-07:00","id":1476674,"title":"","content":"It is my thought that Digital Manipulation beyond 1 dot is there purely for Q-tech or Nova-tech.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24929-econclark","name":"econclark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-20T17:38:55-07:00","id":1476805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1476599-aberrant-tech-control-hacking-in-powers?p=1476637#post1476637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who ever wrote it, didn\u2019t expressed well on out it\u2019s utility or <i><b>it\u2019s utility was cut from the text long before printing.</b></i></div> </div> </div> </div>I've got to believe the latter because the text that is there describes it's utility rather well. It's a rather good &amp; powerful ability well worth a single dot of Mega-Edge expenditure.<br /> <br /> I have to believe that there was more to it that is trimmed out because, extra dots for the purposes of Intellect/Technology substitution is just stupid given it <i><b>cannot</b></i> be higher than Intellect and Technology is far cheaper to buy up as a Skill. Something that makes sense is the idea one could purchase Power Tags with the extra dots. Range makes a lot of sense because, rules as written, this power is only one that can be used at Close (i.e. touch) range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T00:21:01-07:00","id":1476925,"title":"","content":"The only problem with that is that you can just buy the power tags directly, for the same cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T06:45:29-07:00","id":1476952,"title":"","content":"I would fix that with the same fix/language that digital scan uses &quot;if you also have the Telecommunication Mega Edge you can use Digital Scan at Visual Range&quot;. Replace Digital Scan with Digital Manipulation and apply there too. It also makes sense thematically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24929-econclark","name":"econclark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T18:22:36-07:00","id":1477043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1476599-aberrant-tech-control-hacking-in-powers?p=1476925#post1476925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only problem with that is that you can just buy the power tags directly, for the same cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but there are a few places where the Power Tags are mentioned in the Power or Mega-Edge description sort of as a hint or guide to players in how to apply them. I could &quot;maybe&quot; see that as being done here...<br /> <br /> ...but frankly, it looks more like there was more to the power at some point that was cut out without removing the unnecessary dots from the Mega-Edge. The more we look at the maths, and the longer the devs ignore the query in Ask a Dev, the more likely that seems to be the case. \ud83e\udd37<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>econclark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1476599-aberrant-tech-control-hacking-in-powers?p=1476952#post1476952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would fix that with the same fix/language that digital scan uses &quot;if you also have the Telecommunication Mega Edge you can use Digital Scan at Visual Range&quot;. Replace Digital Scan with Digital Manipulation and apply there too. It also makes sense thematically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. Works well, though as Storyguide, I'd be lenient as to what counts as &quot;perception&quot; for a technokinetic styled nova; i.e. they'll be able to affect computers in the same building even if they cannot visually &quot;see&quot; them.<br /> <br /> ...which would once again leads us back to why anyone would ever bother investing more than one dot in the Mega-Edge?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-23T07:06:40-07:00","id":1477086,"title":"","content":"I still think that it is mostly for the Q-tech and nova-tech possibilities. I realize that the builder of the Q-Tech would likely have Technology higher, but that may not be the case for the end user (Starting Q-tech is one example of this, the user doesn't have to be the builder). Q-tech is really great and can be quite powerful, but good inventors will quickly outpace their own ability to utilize the Q-tech (even when you consider mods), thus it is likely that they will either invent for stuff they are interested in and try to sell some of it later to fund future projects or acquire the special materials to complete a current project, or take on contracts to build specific items.<br /> <br /> Regardless, one of the first things that is likely to come out (and maybe even be moved to nova-tech) is a very proficient hacking tool that allows even a novice to hack relatively advanced systems. Like you see in the movies where they just plug in a USB and they are in.<br /> <br /> You can put 5 dots of this on an appropriate q-tech or nova-tech device, but you cannot put a skill on a device.<br /> <br /> It is true that I don't see much of a reason to use the extra dots outside of technology, but that use case alone has always been enough justification to me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As an aside, I just realized that I was reading it slightly wrong with regards to range, I had previously thought that if you had Digital Manipulation, Digital Scan, and Telecommunication, they all worked together at essentially the same range.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24929-econclark","name":"econclark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-14T12:50:46-07:00","id":1481108,"title":"","content":"Having more than one dot of Digital Manipulation available isn't hurting anything, and it gives the very rare, very niche character concept of a Luddite computer controller a decent pool. But in msot other circumstances, don't bother.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\">Community Content Creator</a><a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\"> - OPP Freelancer</a> - Storyguide / Storyteller<br /> Currently Running: Trinity Continuum Core, Vampire the Masquerade 5th Edition","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3331-tragedyjones","name":"tragedyjones","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-19T08:58:22-07:00","id":1481461,"title":"","content":"Another option for this that I have noticed in looking at how to replicate the missing powers from the first edition in the new rules - almost all the \u201cControl a Particular Type of Thing\u201d powers are now gone, with the idea being that you just use Elemental Mastery to build them instead. So there is no more Weather Manipulation, or Gravity Control, or Plant Mastery. All of these just become a version of Elemental Mastery.<br /> <br /> It seems like there is no particular reason you couldn\u2019t do the same thing with Cyberkinesis. It\u2019s just that instead of plants or weather, the element you control is machines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2076-mrapophenia","name":"MrApophenia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-20T05:45:19-07:00","id":1481528,"title":"","content":"You could also use the Machine theme from Quantum Agent, throw on a Restriction to only affect physical machines, and use that to control machinery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-20T06:23:27-07:00","id":1481530,"title":"","content":"Controlling machinery to do what they are intended to, like make a car move or a computer connect to Internet is far easier with just Digital Manipulation, it\u2019s 1 dot and telecommunication you gain not just visual range but also can control radios and telepathy to other novas.<br /> <br /> Quantum Agent would make it more like Magneto controlling robots and making weird constructs to attack people, and less commanding cars and computers.<br /> <br /> Elemental Mastery would be perfect to that end if not for technokinesis becoming a set of Mega Edges instead of a power as used to be. Honestly those mega edges are far more flexible than the old techniques of Cyberkinesis\u2026 if you want a combination of controlling any tech, from mechanical machines to computers, than you may use elemental mastery and set digital mega edges as techniques of it (or ignore, as they cost 1 dot each, and buy them separately), with other techniques being Quantum construct to control/animate tech (transformers style), quantum anima to control their movement directly, Quantum attack to make weapons attack or make electricity come out of the cables, etc, all with the restriction to only working on technological stuff and requiring it to work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T17:07:55-07:00","id":1482204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrApophenia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1476599-aberrant-tech-control-hacking-in-powers?p=1481461#post1481461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another option for this that I have noticed in looking at how to replicate the missing powers from the first edition in the new rules - almost all the \u201cControl a Particular Type of Thing\u201d powers are now gone, with the idea being that you just use Elemental Mastery to build them instead. So there is no more Weather Manipulation, or Gravity Control, or Plant Mastery. All of these just become a version of Elemental Mastery.<br /> <br /> It seems like there is no particular reason you couldn\u2019t do the same thing with Cyberkinesis. It\u2019s just that instead of plants or weather, the element you control is machines.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s a useful way of looking at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}